      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is the one thing drove me from making content while I played on Quest. Switching avatar or world would sometimes cause the debug menu to end up far out of reach without any way to return it. The expression menu also not displaying if it was enabled or not made it incredibly annoying to find it if it did get shot off. On Quest, you must restart the game completely to return the menu to get it back in reach…\n\nThe fact this menu is also not scrollable in VR, highlights completely blue due to no outlines on Quest, and has the fattest hitbox to grab it while i’m attempting to test gestures… made creating content on Quest while I used the debug menu as a crutch while learning the most aggravating thing i’ve experienced in VR.\n\nThe debug menu absolutely crippled my motivation and drive while making content on Quest. To this day, my VRChat Ask profile bio is still just a huge rant about the debug menu, explaining these exact issues and how solutions for them are already implemented in other UI elements. When I was told that the debug menu wasn’t slated for updates when the updated QM UI beta hit, it crushed me.\n\nKnowing the debug menu has not been touched in that time, or really ever since release, I only become resentful of the times the debug menu drove me crazy while I was passionately working on content and ideas in my free time.\n\nI hate the debug menu in its current state.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-01-10T19:30:25.972Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Firstly:\n\nCurrently, the avatar debug menu is a stateless button - it would be awesome if there could be some visual queue in the menu showing us if the debug menu is visible or not :)\n\nSecondly:\n\nOften times when I am testing my work, I go back and forth between my desk and my VR space. After a while I always end up losing where my debug menu is, then I have to physically walk around my VR space to find it. It makes for a good laugh for my friends in world, but it cramps my workflow - it would be great to have a way to reset the debug menu to somewhere visible!",
